centered on such characters, especially, since the 1930s, in American comic books, as well as in Japanese media."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/1e/Front_cover%2C_%22Wow_Comics%22_no._38_%28art_by_Jack_Binder%29.jpg/330px-Front_cover%2C_%22Wow_Comics%22_no._38_%28art_by_Jack_Binder%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Superhero"},{"title":"Hero","blocks":[{"text":"A hero is a real person or fictional character who, in the face of danger, combats adversity through feats of ingenuity, courage, or strength. The original hero type of classical epics did such things for the sake of glory and honor. Post-classical and modern heroes, on the other hand, perform great deeds or selfless acts for the common good instead of the classical goals of wealth, pride, and fame. The antonym of hero is villain. Other terms associated with the concept of hero may include good guy or white hat."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/ba/Achilles_fighting_against_Memnon_Leiden_Rijksmuseum_voor_Oudheden.jpg/330px-Achilles_fighting_against_Memnon_Leiden_Rijksmuseum_voor_Oudheden.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Hero"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/9a/Flame_002.png/330px-Flame_002.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/9a/Flame_002.png/330px-Flame_002.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Fox Feature Syndicate's 1930s–1940s superhero the Flame","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AFlame_002.png"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/20/OutOfTheNightNo11pp34.jpg/500px-OutOfTheNightNo11pp34.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 